  "id": "intensive-psychotherapy",
  "term": "intensive psychotherapy",
  "definition": "Intensive psychotherapy is a short-term, concentrated form of psychotherapy delivered in a highly structured way over a limited period. In this packet, it refers to a model for PTSD that combines a small number of closely supported core sessions with additional non-drug psychotherapy sessions, emphasizing the person’s own capacity for healing and the therapeutic relationship as central to change.",
